st like a few other  girls stoked on it though there's almost  50,000 Instagram but it's not just  online twice a month  gross swirl hosts a group skate in  Venice where dozens of women show up  many for their very first time on wheels  we never actually know how many girls  are going to show up to each group skate  you feel safe as a woman and for us to  have created that space is I think like  I don't know that's what I love the most  most of these girls are in the Venice  area the fact that we were all within  like a couple mile radius and didn't  know about each other and now we've just  like come together it's just I mean it's  amazing the group attracts all ages from  grown women to the youngest  five-year-old Kenny Pollard how fast do  you think you can go on the skateboard  pretty fast if penny could do it your  shoulders and your eyes are your  steering wheel there's no way I could  resist you don't have to like riff you  don't have to do tricks we're just  asking to kick bush we're there to like  support you the whole idea is we're  trying to make this less intimidating  for women when you're a woman alone on  this skateboard it's very different when  you're a woman together with all these  other people you really create Girl  Power Girl Power is real you can change  things in your communities  that community is now global the group  has gotten messages from women as far  away as Italy and Dubai all wanting to  start chapters of their own and now  girls world even has the ultimate symbol  of skater cred  a board of its own built by iconic  skateboard brand Carver only pro  athletes get their own skateboard so if  the fact that our group is getting to  launch one with them is amazing it's  beautiful it is beautiful but not nearly  as beautiful as a sunset skate along the  Venice Boardwalk possible only because  of nine women determined to get everyone  else on board for CBS this morning  Jamie yuccas Los Angeles board was  beautiful absolutely beautiful good for  them you know how to do that no I mean I  in high school I did with skateboarder a  couple times do you join I look at Jamie  I'm thinking it she looks a little like  Nana which is what I would look to on  the skateboard but I admire her for  doing it like Nana that would be me that  would be that's not a knock on Jamie  because that would so be me I admire for  getting up and doing yeah when I was a  kid had a huge massive epic wipeout that  cured me of it for a while and then when  my kids got back into it I tried and you  break that was enough I didn't break  anything I just it was there were a lot  of it was it's really buried deep Thank  You Jamie you good

